WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:01.839
<v Examiner>Taste.

2
00:00:01.839 --> 00:00:02.626
<v Examiner>Five marks.

3
00:00:03.076 --> 00:00:06.058
<v Examiner>Briefly describe the structure of the taste buds,

4
00:00:06.058 --> 00:00:08.857
<v Examiner>and discuss the physiology of taste sensation.

5
00:00:09.307 --> 00:00:12.202
This one is her learning outcome, word for word.

6
00:00:12.202 --> 00:00:16.603
Her quizzes never asked it, which is exactly why it's worth having ready.

7
00:00:17.053 --> 00:00:22.088
The hook: buds on the papillae, chemicals in the saliva, nerves seven, nine and ten,

8
00:00:22.088 --> 00:00:23.347
and up to the insula.

9
00:00:23.797 --> 00:00:26.690
Taste, or gustation, is a chemical sense.

10
00:00:26.690 --> 00:00:32.266
Taste buds are chemoreceptors, stimulated by chemicals dissolved in the saliva.

11
00:00:32.716 --> 00:00:33.579
The structure.

12
00:00:33.579 --> 00:00:35.305
The tongue carries papillae.

13
00:00:35.305 --> 00:00:37.586
Fungiform, which are mushroom-shaped.

14
00:00:37.586 --> 00:00:39.435
Vallate, surrounded by a moat.

15
00:00:39.435 --> 00:00:40.914
Filiform, thread-shaped.

16
00:00:40.914 --> 00:00:42.455
And foliate, leaf-shaped.

17
00:00:42.455 --> 00:00:46.031
The taste buds are specialised structures on the papillae.

18
00:00:46.031 --> 00:00:48.928
Each taste bud is a cluster of gustatory cells,

19
00:00:48.928 --> 00:00:52.380
about fifty to a hundred and twenty-five chemoreceptors,

20
00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:54.660
inside a capsule of supporting cells.

21
00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:57.804
Their gustatory hairs poke out into the taste pore.

22
00:00:58.254 --> 00:01:02.627
Five tastes: sweet, sour, salty, bitter, and umami, which is savoury.

23
00:01:04.077 --> 00:01:04.793
The pathway.

24
00:01:04.793 --> 00:01:07.058
The facial nerve, cranial nerve seven,

25
00:01:07.058 --> 00:01:10.276
carries taste from the front two-thirds of the tongue.

26
00:01:10.276 --> 00:01:13.674
The glossopharyngeal nerve, nine, carries the back third.

27
00:01:13.674 --> 00:01:16.535
And the vagus nerve, ten, carries the very back.

28
00:01:16.535 --> 00:01:21.602
They go to the brain stem, then up to the thalamus, the insula, and the frontal lobe.

29
00:01:21.602 --> 00:01:26.072
The amygdala and the hypothalamus add the emotional response, and appetite.

30
00:01:26.522 --> 00:01:28.242
Flavour is taste plus smell.

31
00:01:28.242 --> 00:01:30.269
Chewing releases aroma molecules,

32
00:01:30.269 --> 00:01:34.261
which travel from the back of the mouth up into the nasal cavity,

33
00:01:34.261 --> 00:01:36.165
and the brain combines the two.

34
00:01:37.615 --> 00:01:38.280
The traps.

35
00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:40.276
Taste buds are chemoreceptors.

36
00:01:40.276 --> 00:01:44.535
One of her true or false statements says they're photoreceptors.

37
00:01:44.535 --> 00:01:44.935
False.

38
00:01:44.935 --> 00:01:47.996
Second: filiform papillae carry no taste buds.

39
00:01:47.996 --> 00:01:49.326
They're for texture.

40
00:01:49.326 --> 00:01:53.319
The buds are on the fungiform, vallate and foliate papillae.

41
00:01:53.319 --> 00:01:56.513
Third: the facial nerve is the front two-thirds,

42
00:01:56.513 --> 00:01:59.375
and the glossopharyngeal is the back third.

43
00:01:59.825 --> 00:02:00.571
<v Examiner>Once more.

44
00:02:00.571 --> 00:02:01.019
<v Examiner>Taste.

45
00:02:03.469 --> 00:02:04.992
Taste is a chemical sense:

46
00:02:04.992 --> 00:02:08.739
taste buds are chemoreceptors for chemicals dissolved in saliva.

47
00:02:08.739 --> 00:02:12.076
They sit on the papillae, fungiform, vallate and foliate,

48
00:02:12.076 --> 00:02:16.116
and each bud is a cluster of gustatory cells in a supporting capsule,

49
00:02:16.116 --> 00:02:18.400
with gustatory hairs in the taste pore.

50
00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:21.328
Five tastes: sweet, sour, salty, bitter and umami.

51
00:02:21.328 --> 00:02:26.187
The facial nerve carries the front two-thirds, the glossopharyngeal the back third,

52
00:02:26.187 --> 00:02:29.759
and the vagus the very back, to the brain stem, the thalamus,

53
00:02:29.759 --> 00:02:31.633
the insula and the frontal lobe.

54
00:02:31.633 --> 00:02:33.272
Flavour is taste plus smell.
